WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
In some markets, a few big
firms make most of the sales.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.800
They fight hard for every customer:

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.740
new designs, loyalty
points, adverts everywhere.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.330
Yet their prices often stay
stable for long periods.

5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.620
If they want more customers,

6
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.140
why not simply cut their prices?

7
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.320
In this mission, you'll follow a
price war between two rival firms,

8
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.580
one step at a time,

9
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.280
and track their profits.

10
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.110
Then you'll see what branding
and loyalty schemes do

11
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.130
to a firm's demand curve.

12
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.100
Your mission: find out
why a few big rivals

13
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.870
so often compete on brand and quality.
